[al:新概念英语第三册]
[ti:15. Sixpence Worth of Trouble]
[00:01.180] Passage 15 | 第15章
[00:02.665] Sixpence worth of trouble | 六便士的麻烦
[00:05.360] Children always appreciate small gifts of money. | 孩子们总是很喜欢小额的钱财礼物。
[00:09.205] Father, of course, provides a regular supply of pocket money, | 父亲当然会定期给零花钱，
[00:13.110] but uncles and aunts are always a source of extra income. | 但叔叔阿姨们总能提供额外的收入。
[00:16.550] With some children, small sums go a long way. | 对一些孩子来说，小额的钱能用很久。
[00:19.985] If sixpences are not exchanged for sweets, | 如果六便士没有被用来买糖果，
[00:22.740] they rattle for months inside money boxes. | 它们就会在存钱罐里叮当作响好几个月。
[00:25.545] Only very thrifty children manage to fill up a money box. | 只有非常节俭的孩子才能把存钱罐装满。
[00:29.060] For most of them, | 对他们中的大多数人来说，
[00:30.175] sixpence is a small price to pay for a satisfying bar of chocolate. | 六便士是买一块令人满足的巧克力所需支付的小额费用。
[00:34.970] My nephew George has a money box, | 我的侄子乔治有一个存钱罐，
[00:38.015] but it is always empty. | 但它总是空的。
[00:39.870] Very few of the sixpences I have given him have found their way there. | 我给他的六便士很少有能存进去的。
[00:44.005] I gave him sixpence yesterday and advised him to save it. | 昨天我给了他六便士，并建议他存起来。
[00:48.215] Instead, | 结果呢，
[00:49.485] he bought himself sixpence worth of trouble. | 他给自己惹了六便士的麻烦。
[00:52.545] On his way to the sweet shop, | 在他去糖果店的路上，
[00:54.770] he dropped his sixpence, | 他把六便士掉了，
[00:56.375] and it rolled along the pavement and then disappeared down a drain. | 它沿着人行道滚下去，然后消失在下水道里。
[01:00.155] George took off his jacket, rolled up his sleeves, | 乔治脱下夹克，卷起袖子，
[01:03.500] and pushed his right arm through the drain cover. | 把右臂伸进了下水道盖子。
[01:06.360] He could not find his sixpence anywhere, | 他到处都找不到他的六便士，
[01:08.805] and what is more, he could not get his arm out. | 更要命的是，他的手臂也拿不出来了。
[01:12.265] A crowd of people gathered round him, | 一群人围在他身边，
[01:14.570] and a lady rubbed his arm with soap and butter. | 一位女士用肥皂和黄油擦他的手臂。
[01:17.155] But George was firmly stuck. | 但乔治被牢牢地卡住了。
[01:19.845] The fire brigade was called, | 消防队被叫来了，
[01:21.970] and two firemen freed George using a special type of grease. | 两名消防员用一种特殊的润滑剂把乔治解救出来。
[01:26.525] George was not too upset by his experience | 乔治并没有因为这次经历而过于沮丧，
[01:29.875] because the lady who owns the sweet shop heard about his troubles | 因为拥有糖果店的那位女士听说了他的麻烦，
[01:33.580] and rewarded him with a large box of chocolates. | 并奖励了他一大盒巧克力。